From a04878021064da6130538845da928d29a366e629 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:53:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] x11: a wheel notch that arrives as buttons is one notch

XInput2 reports a wheel without smooth-scroll valuators as a press and
a release of buttons 4 to 7 for every notch, and xinput2_button_input
turned both into a MouseWheel, so every notch scrolled twice. A real
wheel under libinput does not show it, since its buttons come flagged
XIPointerEmulated and are dropped above; the wheels that do arrive as
plain buttons are XTEST's (xdotool click 5) and those of the X servers
behind VNC and RDP sessions (Xvnc, xrdp), which have no valuators to
give.

Only the press is a notch now, and the release is dropped, as the
0.31 X11 backend does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/changelog/unreleased.md b/src/changelog/unreleased.md
index f3a0f6d..9f1e1b5 100644
--- a/src/changelog/unreleased.md
+++ b/src/changelog/unreleased.md
@@ -39,3 +39,7 @@ The migration guide could reference other migration examples in the current
 changelog entry.
 
 ## Unreleased
+
+### Fixed
+
+- On X11, fix a wheel that arrives as button presses (XTEST, Xvnc, xrdp) scrolling twice per notch.
diff --git a/src/platform_impl/linux/x11/event_processor.rs b/src/platform_impl/linux/x11/event_processor.rs
index 79f5c11..3c8d352 100644
--- a/src/platform_impl/linux/x11/event_processor.rs
+++ b/src/platform_impl/linux/x11/event_processor.rs
@@ -1080,16 +1080,24 @@ impl EventProcessor {
             // those. In practice, even clicky scroll wheels appear to be reported by
             // evdev (and XInput2 in turn) as axis motion, so we don't otherwise
             // special-case these button presses.
-            4..=7 => WindowEvent::MouseWheel {
-                device_id,
-                delta: match event.detail {
-                    4 => MouseScrollDelta::LineDelta(0.0, 1.0),
-                    5 => MouseScrollDelta::LineDelta(0.0, -1.0),
-                    6 => MouseScrollDelta::LineDelta(1.0, 0.0),
-                    7 => MouseScrollDelta::LineDelta(-1.0, 0.0),
-                    _ => unreachable!(),
+            //
+            // A wheel button is pressed and released for every notch, so only the press is a
+            // notch: one that went on both, as this did, scrolled twice as far as the wheel
+            // was turned for every wheel that does arrive as buttons (XTEST, and the X servers
+            // of VNC and RDP sessions, which have no valuators to give).
+            4..=7 => match state {
+                ElementState::Pressed => WindowEvent::MouseWheel {
+                    device_id,
+                    delta: match event.detail {
+                        4 => MouseScrollDelta::LineDelta(0.0, 1.0),
+                        5 => MouseScrollDelta::LineDelta(0.0, -1.0),
+                        6 => MouseScrollDelta::LineDelta(1.0, 0.0),
+                        7 => MouseScrollDelta::LineDelta(-1.0, 0.0),
+                        _ => unreachable!(),
+                    },
+                    phase: TouchPhase::Moved,
                 },
-                phase: TouchPhase::Moved,
+                ElementState::Released => return,
             },
             8 => WindowEvent::MouseInput { device_id, state, button: MouseButton::Back },
 
